From 42274fdb8be4f99d241453d09ec3b8e210521739 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:39:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/40] Test harness: fix false-green and flaky checks

- client_contract.py: state() also treats ProcessLookupError (process reaped
  between open() and read() of /proc/PID/stat) as reaped; was ~20% flaky.
- harness_selftest.py: caught() regex matched the success summary lines of
  every tool, so "recognised" degenerated to "no Traceback"; now only
  violation messages count.
- json_fuzz.py: generator now emits NaN/Infinity/-Infinity; the documented
  constraint was never exercised (a parser accepting them passed).
- random_docs.py: print and check the number of documents actually checked,
  not the command-line argument.

Integration note: the client_contract.py hunk (ESRCH in state()) is dropped: the same fix is already in
from python-client (2550540, which also closes the file); the other three files apply as is.

(cherry picked from commit db72de1751544c50ae376936c839b543983cf7b9)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JgWRtX2jyUidN8gxEhe5qx
